Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is \u201cfinancial point of view\u201d the sole consideration when determining whether an offer is superior?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement: SECTION 8.5. Strategic Considerations. <omitted> (c) During the Pre-Closing Period, the Company Board may modify its recommendation if, and only if, <omitted> (iii) the Company Board determines in good faith, after consultation with the Company’s outside legal counsel and strategic advisors, that the failure to modify its recommendation or terminate this Agreement would be inconsistent with the fiduciary duties of the Company Board under applicable Law, (iv) the Company has provided Parent written notice of its intention to modify its recommendation or terminate this Agreement not earlier than 11:59 p.m. New York time on the third Business Day after Parent receives such written notice and (v) if not in connection with an Intervening Event pursuant to Section 8.5(d), the decision to modify its recommendation is in connection with a Strategic Proposal or with the Company’s intent to terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement, and the Company shall have complied with clauses (1) through (4), as follows: (1) prior to giving effect to clauses (2) through (4), the Company Board shall have determined that such Strategic Proposal is a Superior Proposal, (2) the Company shall have made available to Parent orally and in writing the material terms and conditions of such Strategic Proposal and copies of all written communications (and, if oral, a summary of the material terms of such communications) relating to such Strategic Proposal in accordance with Section 8.5(b), (3) the Company shall have negotiated in good faith with Parent during the three Business Day period provided in the foregoing clause (iv) of this Section 8.5(c) with respect to such proposed revisions to this Agreement or other proposals made by Parent, if any, so that the Strategic Proposal would no longer constitute a Superior Proposal, (4) after considering the results of negotiations with Parent and taking into account the proposals made by Parent, if any, after consultation with its outside legal counsel, strategic advisors, and a financial advisor of nationally recognized reputation, the Company Board shall have determined in good faith that such Strategic Proposal remains a Superior Proposal, and, after consultation with its outside legal counsel, that the failure to modify its recommendation or terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement would be inconsistent with the fiduciary duties of the Company Board under applicable Law. For clarity, the provisions of this Section 8.5(c) shall also apply to any amendment to the financial terms or any other material amendment to any Strategic Proposal (except that any reference to three Business Days shall instead be two Business Days) or any successive Strategic Proposals. (Pages 82-83)\nAnswer:
